silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_01_olog_as_typed_english_sections_01_olog_definition_spivak_kent_concrete_anchor_6_tau_N#typednoungate silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedNounGate is the typing gate that admits the noun-phrase 'a domestic cat' as an O_eng box. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'tau_N', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
